  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The distance between two consecutive points with phase difference of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> in a wave of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The velocity with which wave is travelling is ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "18",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Distance between two consecutive points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;out of phase is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>&#981;</mi></math></p><p>Putting the values, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Now, velocity of wave is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>18000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
